<title>USA: Time Warner expected to order TV boxes - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Time Warner expected to order TV boxes - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Time Warner Inc is expected to announce it will spend between $400 and $450 million for a million new digital TV set-top boxes to offer Internet access as well as more channels, The Wall Street Journal reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scientific-Atlanta Inc is to supply 550,000 of the new boxes and will license its technology to Toshiba Corp and Pioneer Electronic Corp, which will deliver the remaining boxes, the story says.</p>
<p>Time Warner is expected to distribute the boxes to customers by the end of 1997, the story says.</p>
</text>
